const COMMON = `
You are a senior engineer implementing one package of "Studio Assistant": a private web app for a barber studio in Ivanhoe, Victoria, Australia. Core purpose: owner drops phone haircut videos into a project, picks a length/style/music, clicks "Generate 5 edits", gets five genuinely different vertical (9:16) previews, can revise/regenerate each independently (old versions preserved) and export real 1080x1920 MP4s.

REPOSITORY FACTS (read before writing code):
- Root: /home/user/editor (pnpm monorepo, Node 22, TypeScript 5.9 strict + noUncheckedIndexedAccess, ESM, Zod 4, vitest 5, Drizzle 0.45, pg-boss 12, Next.js 16, React 19, Tailwind v4). Dependencies are already installed.
- Read FIRST: /home/user/editor/docs/architecture.md, every file in /home/user/editor/packages/core/src (the contracts: EditPlan schema, validateEditPlan, computeTimeline, STYLES, analysis types, jobs, safe zones, settings, revision hints, music licence), /home/user/editor/packages/db/src/schema.ts, /home/user/editor/packages/storage/src/types.ts and keys.ts, /home/user/editor/packages/queue/src/index.ts, /home/user/editor/packages/config/src/index.ts, /home/user/editor/packages/media/src/ffmpeg.ts and ffprobe.ts.
- Conventions: relative imports inside a package use the ".js" suffix (e.g. import { x } from './foo.js'); workspace packages are imported by name (@studio/core, @studio/db, @studio/storage, @studio/queue, @studio/config, @studio/media, @studio/ai). Each package exports from src/index.ts.
- Commands: pnpm --filter @studio/<pkg> typecheck ; pnpm --filter @studio/<pkg> test (vitest, tests live in <pkg>/test/*.test.ts). Always use ABSOLUTE paths in shell commands; the shell working directory resets between commands.
- Do NOT run a bare "pnpm install". If a new dependency is truly essential, add it with an exact version to the package's package.json and run "pnpm install --filter <pkg>" (npm registry is reachable); prefer no new dependencies.
- Do NOT edit files outside the directories you own (listed below). In particular never edit packages/core, packages/db, packages/storage, packages/queue, packages/config, packages/media/src/ffmpeg.ts or ffprobe.ts. If something you need is missing there, implement a local helper in your package and list the gap under notes_for_integrator.
- Test media: /home/user/editor/data/samples (regenerate with: bash /home/user/editor/scripts/make-sample-footage.sh /home/user/editor/data/samples). Files: sample_a_portrait_sdr.mp4 (1080x1920 H.264, mono AAC tone, 12 s), sample_b_rotated_hevc_hlg.mov (1920x1080 HEVC 10-bit HLG with a -90 display-matrix rotation → displays as 1080x1920 portrait, 10 s, mono audio), sample_c_noaudio_scenes.mp4 (1080x1920, no audio, three hard scene changes at 2 s and 4 s, 6 s), sample_d_tiny.mp4 (1.2 s), sample_music_120bpm.mp3 (40 s click track, beat every 0.5 s). ffmpeg 6.1 and ffprobe are installed with libx264, libx265, libass, zscale/tonemap, xfade, drawtext, loudnorm, ebur128, silencedetect, scdet.
- Fonts for video text: /home/user/editor/assets/fonts (Inter-*.otf and InterDisplay-*.otf, family names "Inter" and "Inter Display").
- Australian English in all user-facing text and comments (colour, favourite, licence, analyse). No placeholders, no TODO comments, no mock logic on production paths, no invented APIs. Every exported function documented with a short JSDoc. Handle errors explicitly. Keep user-facing messages plain and non-technical.
- Finish with real verification: run typecheck and tests, and paste the last ~30 lines of the test output into test_output_tail. Do not claim tests pass unless you ran them.
Return ONLY the structured report.`

const MEDIA_ANALYSIS = `${COMMON}

YOUR PACKAGE: packages/media — directory you own: /home/user/editor/packages/media/src/analysis/** and tests /home/user/editor/packages/media/test/analysis*.test.ts, /home/user/editor/packages/media/test/beats.test.ts. Export everything from /home/user/editor/packages/media/src/analysis/index.ts (already re-exported by the package root). Another agent is implementing src/render/** concurrently — do not touch it.

Use runFfmpeg / runFfmpegCapture / runFfmpegToBuffer (src/ffmpeg.ts) and probeMedia (src/ffprobe.ts). Options objects accept ffmpegPath, signal (AbortSignal) and, where sensible, onProgress. Everything must respect cancellation.

IMPLEMENT (all exported, typed with @studio/core types):
1. makeProxy(inputPath, outputPath, { probe, maxHeight = 960, ffmpegPath?, signal?, onProgress?(fraction 0..1) }): Promise<{ width; height; durationSec }>
   - Rely on FFmpeg's default auto-rotation (do not pass -noautorotate) so rotated iPhone clips come out upright.
   - When probe.video.isHdr apply a tonemap chain to SDR BT.709, e.g. zscale=t=linear:npl=100,format=gbrpf32le,zscale=p=bt709,tonemap=tonemap=hable:desat=0,zscale=t=bt709:m=bt709:r=tv,format=yuv420p — verify it actually runs on sample_b and tune if FFmpeg rejects an option.
   - Scale so height ≤ maxHeight keeping aspect with even dimensions; libx264 preset veryfast crf 26 profile high, yuv420p, -movflags +faststart, keyframe interval 2 s, fps preserved (cap 60); audio: aac 96 kbps 48 kHz when the source has audio, otherwise no audio track. Tag output colour as bt709.
2. makeThumbnail(inputPath, outputPath, { probe, timeSec, width = 540, ffmpegPath? }): JPEG (quality ~3), tonemapped and auto-rotated like the proxy.
3. extractFrames(inputPath, timesSec: number[], outDir, { probe, longEdge = 768, ffmpegPath?, signal? }): Promise<Array<{ timeSec; path; width; height }>> — JPEGs for the vision model (≤ 768 px long edge, q≈3, tonemapped/auto-rotated). Use accurate seeking (-ss before -i) one process per time, or one select-based pass; must be deterministic.
4. detectScenes(inputPath, { probe, threshold = 0.3, minShotSec = 0.8, maxShotSec = 5, ffmpegPath?, signal? }): Promise<Array<{ startSec; endSec }>> — run scene detection on a downscaled stream (scale=320:-2 before select='gt(scene,T)' + showinfo, parse pts_time from stderr, or use the scdet filter). Guarantee full coverage [0, duration], merge shots shorter than minShotSec into neighbours, split shots longer than maxShotSec into equal chunks. On sample_c expect boundaries near 2.0 s and 4.0 s (±0.25 s).
5. measureQuality(inputPath, shots, { probe, sampleFps = 2, width = 160, ffmpegPath?, signal? }): Promise<ShotQuality[]> (one per shot, same order). Decode grey frames once: -vf fps=sampleFps,scale=W:H,format=gray -f rawvideo where you compute H yourself (even, from probe display aspect) so frame boundaries in the buffer are exact. Per frame compute: Laplacian variance (3x3 kernel) → sharpness, mean luma → brightness, luma std → contrast, mean abs diff vs previous frame → motion. Normalise each to 0–1 with documented constants calibrated on synthetic clips (e.g. a gaussian-blurred testsrc must score clearly lower sharpness than the sharp original; a dark clip must flag exposureIssue 'dark'). score = weighted combination (sharpness 0.45, exposure-ok 0.25, contrast 0.15, moderate-motion 0.15; heavy motion penalised). Frames are assigned to shots by timestamp.
6. analyseAudio(inputPath, { probe, ffmpegPath?, signal? }): Promise<AudioAnalysis> — hasAudio false → zeros/false. Otherwise: silencedetect (n=-35dB, d=0.5) → silenceRatio; ebur128 → integratedLoudnessLufs (parse the summary "I:" line; null if unavailable); speech heuristic from decoded 16 kHz mono PCM: 25 ms frames, energy above an adaptive noise floor, zero-crossing rate in a speech-like range, and the ratio of 300–3400 Hz band energy to total (small FFT you implement, radix-2) → fraction of speech-like frames → speechConfidence; speechLikely when confidence ≥ 0.35 and at least 1.5 s of speech-like audio. Pure tones (sample_a) and pink noise (sample_b) must come out speechLikely=false. Document that it is a heuristic.
7. decodePcm(inputPath, { sampleRate = 22050, ffmpegPath?, signal? }): Promise<Float32Array> (mono f32le via pipe).
8. detectBeats(pcm: Float32Array, sampleRate): { bpm: number | null; beatTimesSec: number[]; energy: number[]; energyStepSec: number; confidence: number } — onset strength via spectral flux (frame 1024, hop 512, log-magnitude, half-wave rectified), tempo via autocorrelation of the onset envelope over 60–180 BPM (fold octave ambiguities towards 80–160), beat phase by best comb alignment, beat grid snapped to nearby onsets (±40 ms), energy = RMS per 0.25 s window, confidence from autocorrelation peak prominence (0–1). Return bpm null and an empty grid when confidence < 0.2 (silence/noise).
9. analyseMusic(inputPath, { probe, ffmpegPath?, signal? }): Promise<{ durationSec; bpm; beatTimesSec; energy; energyStepSec; confidence }> composing 7 + 8.
10. assembleShots(assetId, scenes, qualities): Shot[] — ids like \`\${assetId.slice(0, 8)}-s\${index}\`, label 'unknown', labelSource 'heuristic', confidence 0, issues derived from quality ('Soft focus', 'Underexposed', 'Overexposed', 'Heavy camera movement', 'Low contrast'), framing 'unknown', focus null.
11. chooseFrameTimes(shots, { maxFrames }): Array<{ shotId; timeSec }> — midpoint of each shot; when there are more shots than maxFrames prefer higher quality.score while keeping temporal spread.

TESTS (must run in CI without network; generate samples in beforeAll if missing by invoking the sample script; skip gracefully with a clear message only if ffmpeg is absent):
- proxy of sample_b → probeMedia shows 540x960 (or ≤960 high, even), h264, yuv420p, colour transfer bt709 (not arib-std-b67), audio aac 48 kHz; proxy of sample_c has no audio stream.
- detectScenes on sample_c → ≥ 3 shots, boundaries near 2 s and 4 s; full coverage.
- measureQuality: generate (via ffmpeg lavfi) a sharp testsrc2 clip and a gaussian-blurred copy (gblur=sigma=6) → blurred sharpness < 0.5 × sharp; a very dark clip (eq=brightness=-0.45) flags 'dark'.
- analyseAudio on sample_c → hasAudio false; on sample_a → hasAudio true, speechLikely false, loudness is a finite number.
- detectBeats on a synthetic click track you build in-process (120 BPM clicks + low noise, 20 s) → bpm within ±2 of 120 and ≥ 90% of beats within 40 ms of a 0.5 s grid; silence → bpm null. Also analyseMusic on sample_music_120bpm.mp3 → bpm 120±3.
- extractFrames on sample_b at [1, 5] → two JPEGs with portrait dimensions ≤ 768 long edge.
Keep the total test runtime under ~90 s (use short clips / low resolutions).`

const MEDIA_RENDER = `${COMMON}

YOUR PACKAGE: packages/media — directory you own: /home/user/editor/packages/media/src/render/** and tests /home/user/editor/packages/media/test/render*.test.ts. Export everything from /home/user/editor/packages/media/src/render/index.ts (already re-exported by the package root). Another agent implements src/analysis/** concurrently — do not touch it; do not depend on it.

GOAL: turn a VALIDATED EditPlan (packages/core: EditPlanSchema, computeTimeline, validateEditPlan, SafeZone/scaleSafeZone/safeArea, STYLES colour presets, BrandConfig) into a single FFmpeg command that renders a real vertical MP4 from the actual footage, with text rendered by libass from an ASS file you generate.

IMPLEMENT (exported):
1. Types: RenderQuality = 'preview' | 'export'. RenderInputs = { plan: EditPlan; assets: Record<assetId, { path: string; probe: AssetProbe }>; music: { path: string; durationSec: number } | null; transcripts?: Record<assetId, TranscriptSegment[]> (for validation context); quality: RenderQuality; output?: OutputFormat (default VERTICAL_PREVIEW for preview, VERTICAL_1080 for export); brand: { accentColour: string (hex); videoTextStyle: 'minimal'|'bold'|'editorial'; fontHeadline: string; fontBody: string; socialHandle?: string }; fontsDir: string; tmpDir: string; ffmpegPath?; threads?: number; signal?: AbortSignal; onProgress?(fraction: number): void }. RenderResult = { outputPath; durationSec; byteSize; probe: AssetProbe; ffmpegArgs: string[] }.
2. renderEditPlan(inputs, outputPath): Promise<RenderResult> — first re-validate with validateEditPlan (assets durations/hasAudio from probes; music; transcripts; durationBounds = [targetDurationSec*0.5, targetDurationSec*1.6] generous since planners already enforced it) and throw AppError('VALIDATION', ...) with the issues if it fails (defence in depth). Then: write the ASS file into tmpDir, build args with buildRenderCommand, run with runFfmpeg (progress = outTimeSec / timeline.totalDurationSec, clamped), probe the output, return the result. On CancelledError propagate it and delete any partial output file.
3. buildRenderCommand(inputs, outputPath, assPath | null): { args: string[]; filterComplex: string; totalDurationSec: number } — pure and unit-testable:
   - One input per SEGMENT using input-level accurate seeking: -ss <inSec> -t <outSec-inSec> -i <asset path> (plus -i for the music file last). Auto-rotation stays on.
   - Per-segment video chain [k:v] → setpts=PTS-STARTPTS → (if asset HDR) tonemap chain (zscale=t=linear:npl=100,format=gbrpf32le,zscale=p=bt709,tonemap=tonemap=hable:desat=0,zscale=t=bt709:m=bt709:r=tv) → speed: setpts=PTS/speed (after the reset) → fps=<output fps> → scale to COVER the output (scale=W:H:force_original_aspect_ratio=increase) → crop W:H with focus (x = (iw-W)*focusX, y = (ih-H)*focusY, clamped, for framing.mode 'focus'; centred otherwise) → optional zoom: implement as a crop whose size shrinks/grows over the segment's local time t: z(t) = from + (to-from)*t/dur; crop=w='iw/(…)':h='ih/(…)':x='(iw-ow)*fx':y='(ih-oh)*fy' followed by scale=W:H (keep even sizes; expressions must use the crop filter's t) → colour preset via eq (none: nothing; natural: contrast=1.03:saturation=1.05; clean: contrast=1.05:saturation=0.98:brightness=0.01; cinematic: contrast=1.08:saturation=0.92:gamma=0.98; punchy: contrast=1.1:saturation=1.15) → format=yuv420p,setsar=1,settb=AVTB → [v_k].
   - Junction chain across segments: for segment k>0, if transitionIn is null use [prev][v_k]concat=n=2:v=1:a=0[x_k]; else [prev][v_k]xfade=transition=<type>:duration=<d>:offset=<cumulative output time before this segment minus d>[x_k]. Offsets must agree exactly with computeTimeline (same maths), so the final video duration equals timeline.totalDurationSec (±1 frame).
   - Text: after the last junction apply ass=filename=<escaped path>:fontsdir=<escaped fontsDir> (escape ':' '\\\\' ''' and ',' for the filter string; or use the subtitles filter if ass misbehaves) → [vout]. Then -map [vout].
   - Audio: build only what exists. Music: [m:a]atrim=start=<startOffsetSec>:end=<startOffsetSec+total>,asetpts=PTS-STARTPTS,aformat=sample_fmts=fltp:sample_rates=48000:channel_layouts=stereo,volume=<volume>,afade=t=in:st=0:d=<fadeIn>,afade=t=out:st=<total-fadeOut>:d=<fadeOut>[music]; ducking (duckUnderOriginal and any original-sound segment present): chain volume=0.25:enable='between(t,S,E)' per original-sound segment on the music. Original sound for segments with keepOriginalSound (and asset has audio): [k:a]asetpts=PTS-STARTPTS,aformat=…stereo 48k,<atempo chain for speed ≠ 1, factors kept within 0.5–2 per stage>,volume=<originalSound.volume>,adelay=<segment start ms>|<same>,apad[o_k] trimmed with atrim=end=<total>. Mix all with amix=inputs=N:normalize=0:duration=longest, then loudnorm=I=<loudnessTargetLufs>:TP=-1.5:LRA=11 (single pass; note the two-pass upgrade in a comment), aresample=48000, -map [aout] -c:a aac -b:a 192k -ar 48000 -ac 2. If there is no audio at all: -an.
   - Video encoding: preview → -c:v libx264 -preset veryfast -crf 27 -profile:v high -pix_fmt yuv420p; export → -c:v libx264 -preset slow -crf 18 -profile:v high -level 4.2 -pix_fmt yuv420p. Both: -r <fps> -g <2*fps> -bf 2 -colorspace bt709 -color_primaries bt709 -color_trc bt709 -movflags +faststart -t <total> plus -threads <threads> and -filter_threads when threads > 0.
4. buildAssDocument(plan, timeline, output: OutputFormat, safeZone: SafeZone (already scaled to the output size), brand, fonts): string — an ASS (SubStation Alpha v4+) document: [Script Info] with PlayResX/PlayResY = output size, WrapStyle 0, ScaledBorderAndShadow yes; [V4+ Styles]: Headline (Inter Display Bold, size ≈ output.height*0.052, white, black outline 3, shadow 1, alignment 2 or 8 depending on placement with MarginV computed from the safe zone), Subtitle (Inter SemiBold, size ≈ height*0.034), Label (Inter Bold, uppercase-ish small ≈ height*0.03 with letter spacing), Caption (Inter SemiBold ≈ height*0.036, outline 2, bottom of the safe area, max 2 lines, wrap at ~26 characters), Accent variants using brand.accentColour (convert #RRGGBB → &H00BBGGRR). videoTextStyle 'bold' → larger/heavier, 'editorial' → lighter weight with more letter spacing, 'minimal' → defaults. Placement: top → just inside safeZone.top; lower → just above safeZone.bottom (i.e. y = height - bottom - margin), centre → vertical centre; horizontally centred within the safe area (use \\\\pos with explicit x,y and \\\\an alignment so text never enters the margins; account for the right margin by centring on the safe area's centre, not the frame centre). Animations: fade → \\\\fad(250,250); rise → \\\\move(x,y+40,x,y,0,350) + \\\\fad(200,250); pop → \\\\fad(120,200)\\\\t(0,180,\\\\fscx108\\\\fscy108)\\\\t(180,320,\\\\fscx100\\\\fscy100); none → nothing. Escape text ({ } \\\\ and newlines). Times as h:mm:ss.cc. Captions use plan.captions (already validated to come from the transcript).
5. Helpers exported for tests: escapeFilterPath(path), colourToAss(hex), buildSegmentFilter(...), atempoChain(speed).
6. docs: a concise /home/user/editor/packages/media/README.md section "Renderer" (append or create) describing the graph and how to debug (print ffmpegArgs).

TESTS (real FFmpeg; keep runtime < ~2 min by rendering previews at 540x960 and only ONE short export):
- Build a plan from the samples: segments from sample_a (speed 1.5, zoom 1→1.1, keepOriginalSound true), sample_b (HDR rotated; transitionIn fade 0.5), sample_c (transitionIn wipeleft 0.4; framing focus 0.3/0.4), three text overlays (top/lower/centre with different animations and one accent), music = sample_music_120bpm.mp3 with offset 2 s, fades, duckUnderOriginal. Target ≈ 8 s. Render preview → probeMedia: 540x960, h264, yuv420p, transfer bt709, aac 48 kHz 2ch, duration within 0.15 s of computeTimeline total. Render the same plan as export → 1080x1920 and duration check.
- Captions test: add a transcript context and two captions; ensure render succeeds and the ASS contains the caption lines in the Caption style.
- Safe-zone test: render the plan with and without text overlays (preview), extract the frame at a time a 'lower' headline is visible as raw grey (ffmpeg -ss T -i … -frames:v 1 -f rawvideo -pix_fmt gray), diff per pixel: assert a meaningful number of changed pixels inside the safe area and (near) zero changed pixels inside the bottom UI margin band and the right rail band of the (scaled) safe zone.
- No-audio plan (sample_c only, no music, originalSound disabled) → output has no audio stream and render succeeds.
- Cancellation: start a preview render with an AbortController, abort after ~400 ms → rejects with CancelledError and no output file remains.
- buildAssDocument unit test: positions within safe area, colour conversion, escaping.
- buildRenderCommand unit test: xfade offsets equal computeTimeline starts; concat used for null transitions; -t equals total.`

const AI = `${COMMON}

YOUR PACKAGE: packages/ai — you own /home/user/editor/packages/ai/** (package.json already lists @anthropic-ai/sdk 1.6.0, zod 4, pino, @studio/core). Create src/index.ts, src/types.ts, src/pricing.ts, src/factory.ts, src/anthropic/{client,labeler,planner,prompts}.ts, src/rules/{planner,labeler}.ts, src/transcription/{openai,none}.ts and tests in test/.

ANTHROPIC SDK USAGE (verified against the installed SDK; do not invent other methods):
- import Anthropic from '@anthropic-ai/sdk'; import { zodOutputFormat } from '@anthropic-ai/sdk/helpers/zod';
- const client = new Anthropic({ apiKey }); structured output: const res = await client.messages.parse({ model, max_tokens, system: [{ type: 'text', text: SYSTEM, cache_control: { type: 'ephemeral' } }], messages: [{ role: 'user', content: [...blocks] }], output_config: { format: zodOutputFormat(Schema), effort } }); then res.parsed_output (null if parsing failed), res.usage.{input_tokens,output_tokens,cache_read_input_tokens,cache_creation_input_tokens}, res.stop_reason ('end_turn' | 'max_tokens' | 'refusal' | ...; on 'refusal' read res.stop_details?.explanation). Images: { type: 'image', source: { type: 'base64', media_type: 'image/jpeg', data } }. Do NOT send temperature/top_p, do NOT send a thinking parameter (adaptive thinking is the default), do NOT use tool_choice forcing, no assistant prefill. Default models come from env: AI_PLANNER_MODEL (default claude-opus-5-5), AI_VISION_MODEL (default claude-haiku-5-5), AI_PLANNER_EFFORT (low|medium|high). Typed errors: Anthropic.AuthenticationError, Anthropic.RateLimitError, Anthropic.BadRequestError, Anthropic.APIError (check most specific first) → map to AppError codes ('INTEGRATION_NOT_CONFIGURED' for auth, 'RATE_LIMITED', 'PROCESSING_FAILED').
- IMPORTANT: structured outputs support a JSON-schema subset. Write a test that calls zodOutputFormat(PlannerWireSchema) and zodOutputFormat(LabelWireSchema) and asserts it does not throw. If the core EditPlanSchema's numeric min/max/defaults/literals are rejected by the helper, define looser "wire" schemas in src/anthropic/schemas.ts (same field names and enums, plain numbers/strings, no defaults) and rely on validateEditPlan for constraints. Never call the real API in tests: inject a fake client with the same parse() signature.

IMPLEMENT:
1. src/types.ts: AiUsage { provider; model; inputTokens; outputTokens; cacheReadTokens; cacheWriteTokens; durationMs; estimatedCostUsdCents }; FrameForLabelling { assetId; shotId; timeSec; jpegPath; width; height }; ShotLabelResult { shotId; label: SegmentLabel; confidence: number; description: string; framing: 'closeup'|'medium'|'wide'|'unknown'; focus: {x,y}|null; issues: string[] }; interface VisionLabeler { name: string; model: string | null; labelShots(input: { frames: FrameForLabelling[]; context: { clipName: string; clipDurationSec: number; projectNotes: string; clipIndex: number; clipCount: number } }, opts?: { signal?: AbortSignal }): Promise<{ results: ShotLabelResult[]; usage: AiUsage | null }> }; PlannerInput { styleId: StyleId; targetDurationSec: number; analyses: AssetAnalysis[] (shot labels already merged with manual tags by the caller); assets: PlanAssetInfo[]; music: { trackId: string; durationSec: number; bpm: number | null; beatTimesSec: number[]; title: string } | null; preferences: EditingPreferences; brand: BrandConfig; businessName: string; instructions: string (owner's free text for this generation); keepOriginalSound: 'auto'|'always'|'never'; captions: 'auto'|'never'; previousPlan?: EditPlan; revisionInstruction?: string; revisionHints?: RevisionHints; attempt: number (0 = first; regenerate increments); previousErrors?: PlanIssue[] (repair loop) }; interface EditPlanner { name: string; model: string | null; planEdit(input: PlannerInput, opts?: { signal? }): Promise<{ plan: unknown; usage: AiUsage | null; source: 'ai' | 'rules' }> }; interface Transcriber { name: string; transcribe(audioPath: string, opts?: { language?: string; signal? }): Promise<{ provider: string; language: string | null; segments: TranscriptSegment[] }> }.
2. src/pricing.ts: USD per million tokens for claude-opus-5-5 (input 4, output 20, cache read 0.20, cache write 5), claude-sonnet-5-5 (2 / 10 / 0.20 / 2.5), claude-haiku-5-5 (0.10 / 0.50 / 0.01 / 0.125) — mark these as the rates current at implementation time and make the table overridable; unknown model → cost 0 and a flag. estimateCostUsdCents(usage, model).
3. src/rules/planner.ts — RulesPlanner (deterministic, no network). This is also the FALLBACK when no API key is configured, so it must produce five genuinely different, valid plans. Algorithm:
   - Collect usable shots across analyses (quality.score ≥ 0.35 and length ≥ 0.6 s); derive "clips" (sub-ranges) from shots; respect role labels (before, cutting, fade_detail, styling, result, reaction, environment, unknown). Rank by score; keep source order available.
   - Style structures (use STYLES[styleId].pacing/transitions/colourPreset/textDensity): beat_montage: 0.5–1.2 s segments cut on the beat grid (from music beatTimesSec starting at a chosen startOffsetSec aligned to a beat; without music use a 120 BPM grid), hook first (best detail/result shot), interleave process shots, end on the best result shot held ≥ 1.5 s; speed ramps 1.25–1.5 on long process shots only. cinematic_reveal: 3–6 process shots 1.5–3 s with alternating slow push-ins (zoom 1→1.08), dissolve 0.5 s between, fadeblack 0.4 s before a final result shot held 3–5 s with a gentle pull-out. before_after: before shot 2–3 s + label "Before"; 1–3 process bridge shots; wipe/slide to the result held ≥ 3 s + label "After"; align the reveal cut to a beat when music exists. clean_promo: steady highest-score shots 1.5–2.5 s, dissolves 0.5 s, headline = businessName at the start, label = social handle (if set) at the end; no speed ramps. process_story: chronological (before or earliest process → process in source order → result), fades 0.3 s, keep original sound on segments whose source range overlaps transcript speech (when transcripts exist and keepOriginalSound ≠ 'never'), captions copied verbatim from transcript segments mapped to output time (only when captions ≠ 'never').
   - Fit the total to targetDurationSec within ±5 % by scaling segment lengths then trimming, keeping every segment within its source shot bounds and ≥ 0.4 s play time, and transitions short enough for validateEditPlan. Always run validateEditPlan internally and repair (shorten/drop transitions, trim) until it passes; throw AppError('PROCESSING_FAILED') with a clear message only if the footage cannot support the style at all.
   - Distinctness: different opening shots and orders per style; for attempt > 0 rotate the shot selection and opening and vary transitions/text so regenerate is visibly different; never reuse the same source range twice in one plan unless unavoidable.
   - Revision hints (RevisionHints from core; also parse revisionInstruction with parseRevisionInstruction if hints absent): targetDurationSec (absolute, or -1 = 0.75×, -2 = 1.3× of the previous total), emphasiseLabels (more/longer segments of those labels), deemphasiseLabels, transitions restrained/none, pacing faster/slower (×0.75/×1.3 segment lengths, more/fewer segments), text less/none/more, music quieter/louder/none, originalSound on/off, opening label. Start from previousPlan when revising so unrelated choices are preserved.
   - Preferences: pacing, textDensity, transitions ('restrained' → only fade/dissolve/fadeblack), colour, musicVolume, standingInstructions (parsed with parseRevisionInstruction too).
   - Text overlays: short (≤ 40 chars), placed 'lower' or 'top', never overlapping, honest (no claims like "best in Melbourne"; use businessName, "Before"/"After", "Fresh cut", "Skin fade", handle). textDensity none → no text.
   - Output: plan object satisfying EditPlanSchema (version 1, title, description ≤ 280 chars describing the actual edit, rationale, output VERTICAL_1080, audio plan incl. beatAlignment info).
4. src/rules/labeler.ts — HeuristicLabeler: returns each shot as 'unknown' with confidence 0 and issues passthrough (never guesses 'before' or 'reaction').
5. src/anthropic/labeler.ts — AnthropicVisionLabeler: batches ≤ 16 frames per request; content = for each frame an image block then a text block "Frame i: shot <shotId>, t=<time>s"; system prompt describes the barber context and label definitions (before = hair untouched before cutting, cutting = clippers/scissors/razor in action, fade_detail = close-up of blended fade/line-up/taper, styling = product/blow-dry/comb finishing, result = finished haircut clearly shown with no tools, reaction = client looking in the mirror/smiling/talking, environment = shop with no clear subject, other) and insists: when unsure use 'unknown'; never guess 'before' or 'reaction'; description ≤ 20 words; framing; focus point as fractions; issues (blur, bad crop, face cut off, shaky). Structured output = { frames: Array<{ shotId, label, confidence, description, framing, focus: {x,y} | null, issues: string[] }> }. Merge results per shot (highest confidence). Record usage.
6. src/anthropic/planner.ts — AnthropicPlanner: system prompt (cache_control) with the editorial rules: authenticity (only use shots that exist; never invent before/reaction; captions only verbatim from the transcript; text ≤ 60 chars; keep text in the safe zone — the renderer handles placement; restrained transitions; segment bounds inside the clip; total within ±5 % of target; cut on provided beat times; vary opening/order/timing/transitions/text between styles; prefer sharp, well-exposed shots; no repeated footage; keep the haircut authentic — no effects). User content: compact JSON built by src/anthropic/prompts.ts → buildPlannerUserContent(input) with: style brief (STYLES[styleId].brief + pacing), target duration, assets (id, duration, hasAudio, filename), up to 60 shots per project (id, assetId, start, end, label, labelSource, confidence, quality score, description, framing, focus, issues), transcript segments (if any), music (trackId, duration, bpm, up to 80 beat times rounded to 2 dp), preferences, brand/business name/handle, owner instructions, and for revisions: the previous plan, the instruction, parsed hints, and previousErrors from the validator ("fix these"). Ask for the plan via output_config.format = zodOutputFormat(PlannerWireSchema). max_tokens 16000. Handle stop_reason: 'refusal' → AppError('UNSUPPORTED', explanation); 'max_tokens' → retry once with 32000 using client.messages.stream? (if streaming parse is not available in the SDK, retry parse with a larger max_tokens and note the limit). Return { plan: parsed_output, usage, source: 'ai' }. The worker (not you) runs validateEditPlan and re-calls planEdit with previousErrors up to 2 times, then falls back to RulesPlanner — expose this policy as a documented helper planWithRepair(planner, fallback, input, validateFn, { maxRepairs: 2 }) in src/plan-with-repair.ts.
7. src/transcription/openai.ts — OpenAiTranscriber using global fetch + FormData/Blob (Node 22): POST https://api.openai.com/v1/audio/transcriptions with model (default whisper-1), file, response_format=verbose_json, timestamp_granularities[]=segment; Authorization Bearer; map segments → TranscriptSegment; errors → AppError. 25 MB limit: the caller passes a compressed mono audio file. src/transcription/none.ts — NoneTranscriber returns no segments (name 'none').
8. src/factory.ts — createAiProviders(env: Env, logger?) → { planner: EditPlanner (AnthropicPlanner when AI_PROVIDER=anthropic else RulesPlanner), rulesPlanner: RulesPlanner, labeler: VisionLabeler | null (AnthropicVisionLabeler or null — the worker uses HeuristicLabeler when null), transcriber: Transcriber | null, describe(): { plannerName, plannerModel, labelerModel, transcriberName } }.

TESTS: rules planner on a synthetic project (3 analyses with labelled shots incl. before/result/process, transcripts on one) → for each of the five styles a plan that passes validateEditPlan with duration bounds target ±15 %, five plans mutually different (different opening segment or order), attempt 1 differs from attempt 0, hints ("make this 15 seconds", "remove the flashy transitions", "show more of the fade") change the plan accordingly; no captions when no transcript; before_after refuses when no 'before' label. Anthropic planner/labeler with a fake client: builds request (system cached, images present, output_config present), handles parsed_output, refusal, usage/cost. Pricing test. zodOutputFormat schema compile test.`

